{
  "raw": {
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/07/F2609-JA.pdf": {
      "title": "Instructional Faculty, Elementary Education—Literacy Focus",
      "description": "Instructional Faculty, Elementary Education—Literacy Focus.  \n \nInstructional Faculty – Education Literacy \n \nRecruitment #: F2609 \nReview Date:  Open | Open until filled \nDepartment:  Division of Education and Leadership \nSalary Rate:   $42,000 - $50,000 \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s lush \nWillamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem, the state’s capital and about 75 minutes from \nPortland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into the state \nsystem as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in \narts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class sizes, a focus on sustainability \nand a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. Western is a Hispanic Serving \ninstitution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students of color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nWestern Oregon University's College of Education invites applications for a full-time Instructional Faculty \nposition in Elementary Education with a Literacy focus. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate \nand/or graduate courses, advise students, and contribute to service activities within the Division of Education \nand Leadership, the College of Education, and the university. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred qualifications. \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you meet the \nfollowing: \n● Master’s degree Education, Curriculum and Instruction, Literacy \n● 1-2 years Demonstrated teaching experience in higher education In Education, Curriculum and \nInstruction, Literacy; especially Elementary Education. XXX \n● 3-5 years Successful experience in K12 teaching (Required) \n● Professional Communication:  Demonstrate clear, respectful, effective written, verbal, and signed \ncommunication with colleagues, students, community members, staff, and other university personnel.  \n● Professional Conduct & Confidentiality:  Maintain professionalism in all interactions while safeguarding \nconfidential information and adhering to FERPA requirements.  \n● Independent Work & Initiative:  Perform responsibilities independently, demonstrating initiative, sound \njudgment, and accountability in completing tasks.  \n● Teamwork & Adaptability:  Collaborate effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds and work \nstyles while remaining flexible and responsive to evolving priorities, needs, and goals. \n \nHow to Apply: Please upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please include \nonly the materials listed below: \n1. WOU Employment Application form  \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the required qualifications \n \n \n \n \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Reference form available here \n \nBackground and Education Verification: \nAs a condition of employment, the selected candidate must successfully complete a criminal background \ncheck. For positions that require a formal degree as a minimum qualification, the university will also verify \neducational credentials. \nBenefits:    \nWestern Oregon University offers an excellent benefits package for eligible employees which includes 95% \npremium paid healthcare, a generous retirement and vacation package, and reduced tuition rates for \nemployees, spouse or dependent at any of the Oregon Public Universities. http://www.wou.edu/hr/benefits/ \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, \nnational origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran status, or any other \ncharacteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our diverse team is a strength that \ndrives our success.   \n \nRequests for Accommodation: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. Applicants who need disability-related accommodations to participate in the application or hiring \nprocess are encouraged to contact leaveandaccommodations@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. Preference \nwill be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and electronically attach the \nrequired documentation at the time of application. For information regarding Veterans' Preference \nqualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nDue to the high volume of applications we receive, we are unable to provide individual updates on application \nstatus. Applicants are encouraged to regularly check the status of the search through the WOU employment \nwebsite. We appreciate your interest in employment at Western Oregon University and thank you for \nconsidering WOU as your employer. \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/07/F2608-JA.pdf": {
      "title": "Instructional Faculty, Teacher Education – Math and Science",
      "description": "Instructional Faculty, Teacher Education – Math and Science.  \n \nInstructional Faculty, Teacher Education – Math and Science \n \nRecruitment #: F2608 \nReview Date: Open | Open until filled \nDepartment:  Division of Education and Leadership \nSalary Rate:   $42,000 - $50,000 \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s \nlush Willamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem, the state’s capital and about 75 \nminutes from Portland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into \nthe state system as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and \ngraduate degrees in arts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class \nsizes, a focus on sustainability and a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. \nWestern is a Hispanic Serving institution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students of color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nThis position serves in the Education and Leadership Division in the College of Education (COE) at Western \nOregon University (WOU) as a full-time instructional faculty member in Teacher Education-Math and Science \nfocus. The Instructional Faculty, Teacher Education-Math and Science, is primarily dedicated to undergraduate \nand graduate instruction (80% effort), encompassing lecture and applied theory in preparation for licensure \ncourses in mathematics and science methods, especially focused on the implementation of effective STEM \ninstruction in K12 classrooms with teaching responsibilities distributed across elementary and secondary \nundergraduate and graduate student populations. Service responsibilities (5% effort) include consistent \nparticipation in undergraduate team meetings as well as monthly Division meetings. Click here for the complete \nposition description which includes knowledge areas and preferred qualifications.  \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred \nqualifications. \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you \nmeet the following: \n● Master’s Degree in Education, Curriculum and Instruction, Math and /or Science \n● Higher Education Teaching Experience: 1–2 years of teaching experience in a higher \neducation setting.  \n● K–12 Teaching Experience: 3–5 years of successful teaching experience in K–12 education.  \n● Professional Communication: Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively through written, \nverbal, and signed interactions with students, colleagues, staff, and community members.  \n● Professional Conduct & Confidentiality: Consistently maintain professionalism, uphold \nconfidentiality, and comply with FERPA and institutional policies.  \n● Independent Work & Initiative: Proven ability to work independently, take initiative, exercise \nsound judgment, and complete responsibilities with minimal supervision.  \n \n \n \n \n● Teamwork & Adaptability: Effectively collaborate with diverse teams, adapt to changing \npriorities, and contribute to a positive, inclusive work environment.  \n● Teaching License Eligibility: Eligible for a professional teaching license, with a current teaching \nlicense, a license that expired within the past five years, or an equivalent current or recently \nheld (within five years) teaching credential.  \n● Professional Licensure: Hold or have recently held (within the past five years) a Math and/or \nScience teaching license or equivalent endorsement. \n \nHow to Apply: Please upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please \ninclude only the materials listed below: \n1. WOU Employment Application form  \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the required qualifications \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Reference form available here \n \nBackground and Education Verification: \nAs a condition of employment, the selected candidate must successfully complete a criminal \nbackground check. For positions that require a formal degree as a minimum qualification, the \nuniversity will also verify educational credentials. \nBenefits:    \nWestern Oregon University offers an excellent benefits package for eligible employees which includes \n95% premium paid healthcare, a generous retirement and vacation package, and reduced tuition \nrates for employees, spouse or dependent at any of the Oregon Public Universities. \nhttp://www.wou.edu/hr/benefits/ \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, \ncolor, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran \nstatus, or any other characteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our \ndiverse team is a strength that drives our success.   \n \nRequests for Accommodation: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. Applicants who need disability-related accommodations to participate in the application \nor hiring process are encouraged to contact leaveandaccommodations@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. \nPreference will be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and \n \n \n \n \nelectronically attach the required documentation at the time of application. For information regarding \nVeterans' Preference qualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nDue to the high volume of applications we receive, we are unable to provide individual updates on \napplication status. Applicants are encouraged to regularly check the status of the search through the \nWOU employment website. We appreciate your interest in employment at Western Oregon University \nand thank you for considering WOU as your employer. \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/07/F2607-JA.pdf": {
      "title": "Instructional Faculty, Interpreting Studies",
      "description": "Instructional Faculty, Interpreting Studies.  \n \nInstructional Faculty, Interpreting Studies \n \nRecruitment #: F2607 \nReview Date:  Open | Open until filled \nDepartment:  Interpreting / DSPS \nSalary Rate:   $42,000 - $50,000 \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s lush \nWillamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem, the state’s capital and about 75 minutes from \nPortland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into the state \nsystem as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in \narts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class sizes, a focus on sustainability \nand a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. Western is a Hispanic Serving \ninstitution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students of color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nThis position serves in the Deaf Studies and Professional Studies (DSPS) Division in the College of Education \n(COE) at Western Oregon University (WOU) as a full time instructional faculty member in Interpreting Studies. \nPrimary responsibilities may include all or a combination of the following duties: teaching within the Interpreting \nStudies programs at WOU (undergraduate and/or graduate); academic advising of students; and service to \none or more of the programs in the DSPS Division, COE, and WOU. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred qualifications. \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you meet the \nfollowing: \n● Master’s Degree in Interpreting, interpreter education or related field \n● Demonstrated teaching experience in higher education In interpreting, interpreter education or related \nfield  \n● Professional Communication: Demonstrates effective written, verbal, and signed communication with \ncolleagues, students, community members, staff, and other university personnel.  \n● Professional Conduct & Confidentiality: Maintains professionalism in all interactions, safeguards \nconfidential information, and collaborates with others in compliance with FERPA requirements.  \n● Independent Work & Initiative: Demonstrates the ability to work independently, take initiative, exercise \nsound judgment, and complete responsibilities with minimal supervision.  \n● Teamwork & Adaptability: Collaborates effectively with individuals representing diverse backgrounds, \nwork styles, and needs while adapting to changing priorities, goals, and organizational requirements \n \nHow to Apply: Please upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please include \nonly the materials listed below: \n1. WOU Employment Application form  \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the required qualifications \n \n \n \n \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Reference form available here \n \nBackground and Education Verification: \nAs a condition of employment, the selected candidate must successfully complete a criminal background \ncheck. For positions that require a formal degree as a minimum qualification, the university will also verify \neducational credentials. \nBenefits:    \nWestern Oregon University offers an excellent benefits package for eligible employees which includes 95% \npremium paid healthcare, a generous retirement and vacation package, and reduced tuition rates for \nemployees, spouse or dependent at any of the Oregon Public Universities. http://www.wou.edu/hr/benefits/ \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, \nnational origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran status, or any other \ncharacteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our diverse team is a strength that \ndrives our success.   \n \nRequests for Accommodation: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. Applicants who need disability-related accommodations to participate in the application or hiring \nprocess are encouraged to contact leaveandaccommodations@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. Preference \nwill be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and electronically attach the \nrequired documentation at the time of application. For information regarding Veterans' Preference \nqualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nDue to the high volume of applications we receive, we are unable to provide individual updates on application \nstatus. Applicants are encouraged to regularly check the status of the search through the WOU employment \nwebsite. We appreciate your interest in employment at Western Oregon University and thank you for \nconsidering WOU as your employer. \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/10/F2613-Job-Announcement-2.pdf": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor, Exercise Science",
      "description": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor, Exercise Science.  \n \nTenure Track Assistant Professor, Exercise Science \n \nRecruitment #: F2613 \nReview Date:  Open | Open until filled \nDepartment:  Division of Health and Exercise Science \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with experience and qualifications \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s lush \nWillamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem, the state’s capital and about 75 minutes from \nPortland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into the state \nsystem as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in \narts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class sizes, a focus on sustainability \nand a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. Western is a Hispanic Serving \ninstitution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students of color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nWestern Oregon University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in our \nExercise Science program housed in the Division of Health and Exercise Science. We are seeking applicants \nwith a background in biomechanics, anatomical kinesiology and other areas relevant to exercise science. \nFaculty may also teach core undergraduate courses and electives in the Exercise Science major.  \n \nThe successful applicant would join a dynamic, student-centered, and collegial division with six other tenure-\ntrack faculty and several instructional faculty (please see our website at https://wou.edu/hexs/). Position duties \nwould entail teaching three 4-credit courses per term with a primary responsibility for Biomechanics and \nAnatomical Kinesiology, and electives in the applicant’s specialty areas. Engaging in high-impact educational \npractice, regular exercise science-related scholarship, and providing meaningful service to the division, \nuniversity and profession is expected. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred qualifications. \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you meet the \nfollowing: \n● Earned Doctorate (Ph.D., Dr. P.H., or Ed.D.) in exercise science, kinesiology, or closely related field (e.g. \nDPT) is required (ABD considered if degree requirements are completed prior to September 16, 2027).  \n● Teaching experience in higher education at the graduate and/or undergraduate level \n● Experience building relationships with community partners \n● Understanding exercise science topics related to improving health, quality of life, and/or \nfitness/performance \n● Experience in student mentorship \n● Evidence of productive scholarship \n \nHow to Apply: Please upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please include \nonly the materials listed below: \n \n \n \n \n1. WOU Employment Application form  \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the required qualifications \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Reference form available here \n \nBackground and Education Verification: \nAs a condition of employment, the selected candidate must successfully complete a criminal background \ncheck. For positions that require a formal degree as a minimum qualification, the university will also verify \neducational credentials. \n \nBenefits:    \nWestern Oregon University offers an excellent benefits package for eligible employees which includes 95% \npremium paid healthcare, a generous retirement and vacation package, and reduced tuition rates for \nemployees, spouse or dependent at any of the Oregon Public Universities. http://www.wou.edu/hr/benefits/ \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, \nnational origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran status, or any other \ncharacteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our diverse team is a strength that \ndrives our success.   \n \nRequests for Accommodation: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. Applicants who need disability-related accommodations to participate in the application or hiring \nprocess are encouraged to contact leaveandaccommodations@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. Preference \nwill be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and electronically attach the \nrequired documentation at the time of application. For information regarding Veterans' Preference \nqualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/03/F-PSY-POOL-2026-JOB-ANNOUNCEMENT.pdf": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Psychology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Psychology.  \nUpdated 4/29/25 \n \nAdjunct Faculty - Psychology [POOL] \n \nRecruitment #: F-PSY \nReview Date:  Ongoing | As needed \nDepartment:  Psychology \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with experience and qualifications [CBA]  \n \nDepartment/Position Summary: \nThe Department of Psychological Sciences in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Western Oregon \nUniversity invites qualified applications for part-time instructional faculty positions to teach undergraduate \ncourses in psychology. These positions are part of a faculty applicant pool intended to support the \ndepartment’s instructional needs on an ongoing basis. \nThe department is seeking candidates with expertise in areas such as General Psychology, Life-Span \nDevelopment, Social Psychology, Research Methods, Cognitive Psychology, Industrial/Organizational \nPsychology, Quantitative Methods, and other specialty topics. Applicants with a PhD are preferred, though \nthose with a master’s degree and relevant experience will be considered. Priority will be given to candidates \nwith previous teaching experience in higher education. \nThe faculty hired through this pool will join a collaborative and student-focused department committed to \nacademic excellence and inclusive teaching practices. The Department of Psychological Sciences offers a \nrigorous curriculum grounded in scientific research and application, preparing students for a wide range of \ncareers and graduate study. For more information about the department and its programs, please visit:  \nhttps://wou.edu/psychology/. \nRequired Qualifications: \n● Master’s Degree or PhD in Psychology or a related field \nHow to Apply: To apply for this position, please upload the following required materials within the application \nportal. Applications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please \ninclude only the materials listed below: \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n \nContact Information: For information regarding this position, contact Rob Winningham, Interim Division \nChair, at winninr@wou.edu or 503-838-8297  \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are processed \nfor positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, \nnational origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran status, or any other \n \n \n \n \ncharacteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our diverse team is a strength that \ndrives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU activity or \nevent, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. If you have \nquestions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. Preference \nwill be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and electronically attach the \nrequired documentation at the time of application. For information regarding Veterans' Preference \nqualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay informed about the progress of this search, we invite and encourage you to explore our career page at \nwou.edu/hr/employment/jobs/. Unfortunately, due to the volume, it is challenging for us to offer individual \nupdates on the status of each application, and for that, we sincerely regret any inconvenience. We thank you \nfor your patience and interest in employment at Western Oregon University. \n \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/05/FBUS-JA.pdf": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Business",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Business.  \n \nAdjunct Faculty – Business/Economics \n \nRecruitment #: F-BUS \nReview Date: Review as needed | Ongoing \nDepartment:  Business & Economics \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with education and experience  \n \nDepartment/ Position Summary: \nWestern Oregon University Invites applications for Adjunct Business and Economics Faculty with a \ncommitment to undergraduate education. Possible areas for courses to be taught include Accounting, Finance, \nMarketing, Economics, Management, Operations and Production, Entrepreneurship, and Quantitative Business \nMethods, as related to an applicant's areas of specialization. Candidates with degrees in a variety of business-\nrelated fields are welcome to apply. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred \nqualifications. \n \nPlease Note: This is a pool position, which means applications are accepted on an ongoing basis to \nbuild a qualified candidate pool. Selected applicants may be contacted as openings become \navailable. \n \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you \nmeet the following: \n● Master’s degree in Business, Economics or related field \n● 1-2 years’ experience Teaching experience in Political Science, Public Policy, Public \nAdministration or related field OR combination of teaching experience and related professional \nexperience \n● Strong verbal and written communication skills \n● Engaging and dynamic classroom instruction \n● Ability to build positive rapport with students \n● Student-centered teaching approach that fosters participation and learning \n \nHow to Apply:  \nPlease upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \n \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please \ninclude only the materials listed below: \n \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n5. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned. Official transcripts will be required if \nhired. \n \nBackground/Education Check: \n \n \n \n \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are \nprocessed for positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, \ncolor, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran \nstatus, or any other characteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our \ndiverse team is a strength that drives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU \nactivity or event, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. \nIf you have questions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. \nPreference will be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and \nelectronically attach the required documentation at the time of application. For information regarding \nVeterans' Preference qualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay updated on the progress of this search, we encourage you to visit our Careers page. Due to \nthe high volume of applications we receive, we're unable to provide individual updates—but please \nknow that your interest is genuinely appreciated. We sincerely thank you for your patience and for \nconsidering a future with Western Oregon University. \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2025/04/F-PRL-POOL-JOB-ANNOUNCEMENT.pdf": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Principal Licensure",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Principal Licensure.  \n \nAdjunct Faculty - Principal Licensure [POOL]  \n \nRecruitment #: F-PRL \nReview Date:  Review as needed | Ongoing \nDepartment:  Education & Leadership / Principal Licensure Pathway \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with education and experience in accordance with [WOUFT CBA] \n \nDepartment/ Position Summary: \nThe Division of Education and Leadership (DEL) in the College of Education at Western Oregon University \ninvites qualified applications for the part-time adjunct faculty positions in the Principal Licensure Pathway (PLP) \nto teach academic classes for PLP candidates and/or supervise PLP candidates in K-12 clinical experiences. \n \nDEL is looking for applicants who are experienced building-level and/or district-level administrators interested \nin helping to prepare school principals by providing them with the necessary knowledge and skills to effectively \nlead a school, including curriculum development, staff management, student discipline, budget oversight, \ncommunity engagement, and legal compliance, all while aligning with state-specific requirements to obtain a \nprincipal license. \n \nCandidates will join a rapidly growing and dynamic Principal Licensure Pathway (PLP) dedicated to inclusive \npractices, social justice, and diversity. The PLP offers courses that prepare current educators for an Oregon K-\n12 Building Principal Licensure and enable candidates to simultaneously earn a master’s degree in education. \nOur PLP also offers Teacher Leader courses for those interested in expanding understanding of Teacher \nLeadership but who might not be ready for the full licensure option. The PLP is part of the Division of Education \n& Leadership in the College of Education, nationally recognized for its leadership in evidence-based teacher \npreparation.  \n \nPlease Note: This is a pool position, which means applications are accepted on an ongoing basis to build a \nqualified candidate pool. Selected applicants may be contacted as openings become available. \n \nResponsibilities: \n● Teach graduate level classes in potentially in-person and/or online/hybrid, synchronous and/or \nasynchronous formats, with possible opportunities for summer, on-campus, and off- campus teaching \n● Participate in curriculum review and development, including activities related to accreditation and \npathway delivery \n● Collaborate in the growth of the PLP \n● Complete a required WOU online training course for effective online and hybrid instructional practices. \n● Must be done prior to the start of teaching or simultaneously during the first term of teaching. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred qualifications. \n \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you meet the \nfollowing: \n● Master’s degree in education or a related field \n● Holds or is eligible for an Oregon teaching and administrative/principal license \n● Minimum five years of experience as a building or district-level administrator \n● At least three years of successful teaching experience \n● Proven knowledge in school leadership, curriculum development, staff management, student discipline, \nbudgeting, community engagement, and legal compliance \n \nHow to Apply:  \n \n \n \n \nTo apply for this position, please upload the following required materials within the application portal. \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please include \nonly the materials listed below: \n \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n5. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned. Official transcripts will be required if hired. \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are processed \nfor positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, \nnational origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran status, or any other \ncharacteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our diverse team is a strength that \ndrives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU activity or \nevent, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. If you have \nquestions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. Preference \nwill be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and electronically attach the \nrequired documentation at the time of application. For information regarding Veterans' Preference \nqualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay updated on the progress of this search, we encourage you to visit our Careers page. Due to the high \nvolume of applications we receive, we're unable to provide individual updates—but please know that your \ninterest is genuinely appreciated. We sincerely thank you for your patience and for considering a future with \nWestern Oregon University. \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/06/F-SUS-2025-JOB-ANNOUNCEMENT.pdf": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Sustainability",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Sustainability.  \n \nAdjunct Faculty - Sustainability [POOL]  \n \nRecruitment #: F-SUS \nReview Date:  Review as needed | Ongoing \nDepartment:  Sustainability \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with education and experience  \n \nDepartment/ Position Summary: \nThe Adjunct Faculty Member in the Department of Sustainability will be responsible for providing \nhigh-quality, learner-centered education in topics in Sustainability. Primary responsibilities include \ndesigning, delivering, and managing courses, while fostering an inclusive and supportive learning \nenvironment. Faculty are expected to demonstrate subject matter expertise, employ effective \nteaching approaches, and maintain professional standards in student engagement and course \nmanagement. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred \nqualifications. \n \nPlease Note: This is a pool position, which means applications are accepted on an ongoing basis to build a \nqualified candidate pool. Selected applicants may be contacted as openings become available. \n \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you meet the \nfollowing: \n● Master’s Degree or PhD in Sustainability or related field.  \n● 1-2 years of teaching experience in Political Science, Public Policy, Public Administration or related \nfield OR combination of teaching experience and related professional experience \n● Communication (verbal and written): Demonstrates clear, professional, and effective communication in \nboth verbal and written interactions, ensuring students understand expectations, instructions, and \nfeedback.  \n● Engaging and dynamic classroom teaching: Uses a variety of instructional strategies and interactive \nactivities to create an engaging learning environment that promotes student participation and critical \nthinking.  \n● Positive rapport with students: Builds respectful, supportive relationships with students and fosters a \nwelcoming classroom environment where students feel valued, comfortable, and motivated to learn. \n \nHow to Apply:  \nTo apply for this position, please upload the following required materials within the application portal. \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration.  \n \nPlease include only the materials listed below: \n \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n5. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned. Official transcripts will be required if hired. \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are processed \nfor positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \n \n \n \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, \nnational origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran status, or any other \ncharacteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our diverse team is a strength that \ndrives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU activity or \nevent, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. If you have \nquestions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. Preference \nwill be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and electronically attach the \nrequired documentation at the time of application. For information regarding Veterans' Preference \nqualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nContact Information \nFor questions regarding the application process or to submit your application documents, please contact \nHuman Resources at employment@wou.edu \n "
    }
  },
